course: dictionary
lesson: 13824
title: Who gives it out?
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: An issuer is a person, company or government that gives out something official. Think of the word issue, which means to give out. The issuer is the one doing the giving.
explain: «The card issuer sent Mia a new card in the post.» The bank is the issuer, because it gives out the card. Mia receives the card, so she is not the issuer.
explain: «The government is the issuer of passports.» Clues: a passport is an official document, and an official body hands it out. So an issuer is the one who makes and gives out something official.
explain: Small print on cards, tickets and forms often names the issuer. When you see it, you can check who gave the thing out.
fact: An issuer is a person, company or government that gives out something official.
fact: Things an issuer can give out include cards, tickets, passports, money and shares.
fact: «The card issuer» is the bank behind a credit card.
fact: A government is the issuer of coins and passports.
fact: Issuer is a formal word, so you will often find it in instructions and small print.
exercise: «The bank is the card issuer for Sam's new credit card.» Who is the issuer? | The shop where Sam buys things | The card reader | *The bank | Sam
exercise: What does issuer mean? | *A person, company or government that gives out something official | A person who spends money in a shop | A ticket for a train | A child who has lost a passport
exercise: «The government is the issuer of coins.» Who gives out the coins? | The bus driver | The shopkeeper | *The government | The children who collect them
test: «The train company is the issuer of the tickets.» What does issuer mean in this sentence? | A paper ticket with a number | The one who uses the tickets to ride | *The one who gives out the tickets | The ticket inspector who checks them
test: Which of these is an issuer? | *A government that gives out passports | A museum visitor | A child who holds a passport | A passenger on a plane
exam: Dad reads the small print: «The issuer of this card is a bank.» Who is the issuer? | The shop | The card | *The bank | Dad
